{"tool_name":"amanida","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"amanida","home":"https://github.com/mariallr/amanida","summary":"An R package for Meta-analysis of metabolomics non-integral data.","addition_date":"2021-12-10T07:47:28.527803Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T20:14:38.697166Z","tool_type":["Library"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:amanida","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"maria.llambrich@urv.cat","name":"Maria Llambrich","typeEntity":"Person"},{"email":"raquel.cumeras@urv.cat","name":"Raquel Cumeras","typeEntity":"Person"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"public"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Quantification","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3799"},{"term":"Standardisation and normalisation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3435"},{"term":"Visualisation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0337"}]}],"name":"Amanida","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"Chan019","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/btab591","metadata":{"abstract":"Summary: The combination, analysis and evaluation of different studies which try to answer or solve the same scientific question, also known as a meta-analysis, plays a crucial role in answering relevant clinical relevant questions. Unfortunately, metabolomics studies rarely disclose all the statistical information needed to perform a meta-analysis. Here, we present a meta-analysis approach using only the most reported statistical parameters in this field: P-value and fold-change. The P-values are combined via Fisher's method and fold-changes by averaging, both weighted by the study size (n). The amanida package includes several visualization options: a volcano plot for quantitative results, a vote plot for total regulation behaviours (up/down regulations) for each compound, and a explore plot of the vote-counting results with the number of times a compound is found upregulated or downregulated. In this way, it is very easy to detect discrepancies between studies at a first glance.","authors":[{"name":"Brezmes J."},{"name":"Correig E."},{"name":"Cumeras R."},{"name":"Guma J."},{"name":"Llambrich M."}],"citationCount":13,"date":"2022-01-15T00:00:00Z","journal":"Bioinformatics","title":"Amanida: an R package for meta-analysis of metabolomics non-integral data"},"pmcid":"PMC8722753","pmid":"34406360"}],"topic":[{"term":"Metabolomics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3172"},{"term":"Preclinical and clinical studies","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3379"},{"term":"Small molecules","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0154"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"Amanida","home":"https://bio.tools/amanida","summary":"An R package for Meta-analysis of metabolomics non-integral data.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:amanida/lib/github.com","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"binaries":{"freeness":null,"registration":null},"packages":null,"source_packages":false,"sourcecode":{"free":true,"interpreted":true,"license":false,"public":true,"readme":true,"repository":{"anonymous":true,"online":true}}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":18,"citations":[{"count":1,"year":"2021"},{"count":2,"year":"2024"},{"count":2,"year":"2025"},{"count":3,"year":"2022"},{"count":5,"year":"2023"},{"count":5,"year":"2026"}],"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/btab591","pmcid":"PMC8722753","pmid":"34406360","ref_count":21,"refs":[{"count":1,"year":"2003"},{"count":1,"year":"2007"},{"count":1,"year":"2009"},{"count":1,"year":"2016"},{"count":3,"year":"2021"},{"count":4,"year":"2018"},{"count":5,"year":"2019"},{"count":5,"year":"2020"}],"title":"Amanida: an R package for meta-analysis of metabolomics non-integral data.","year":2022}]}],"readme":true,"summary":{"description":true},"we